    "body": "## Current question: after the completed B08 comparison\r\n\r\nDoes any specifically justified new B/EXPLORE question remain beyond the common-policy/low-regret result at the original .0025 margin, or should Convergence retain the prior selected-panel family boundary with concrete scientific yield?\r\n\r\nB08 is complete and its P71 diagnostic intake is accepted. All three arms at both33/258 choose the same native actions, with regret .0021294544930598857. New RAW-LONG is KEEP8/8 but REPLAN5/8: the exact-count qualifier fails. Delta_R and Delta_D are0 at both endpoints. Historical RAW improvements are +.0044524264964700775 SHORT and +.0016519755926440258 LONG, retaining3 and2 loss rows and negative REPLAN mean changes. This is weak-new-RAW diagnostic evidence, not a competent negative or an alignment success.\r\n\r\nAgainst this recorded new RAW, even zero treatment regret cannot yield the original .0025 gain: the arithmetic ceiling is .0021294544930598857. That outcome-informed fact does not authorize a weaker comparator, lower MEI, seed/panel search, or treating exact-action repair as sufficient. Native improvement and its losses remain evidence against broad failure claims.\r\n\r\nFixed P71 intake: https://github.com/CartmanFatass/My-paper-code/blob/601d9d8f0612461f4c04ef5f855a9ddd2aed9cee/docs/research/candidates/commitment_residual_triggered_options/CRTO_NATIVE_COST_B08_P71_INTAKE_20260908.md\r\n\r\nFixed P71 original result: https://github.com/CartmanFatass/My-paper-code/blob/8ea7fa71622f8f436b87fbeb3beee0b3b918fc67/docs/research/candidates/commitment_residual_triggered_options/CRTO_NATIVE_COST_B08_P71_RESULT_20260908.json\r\n\r\nPrior complete direction decision: https://github.com/CartmanFatass/My-paper-code/blob/febfad9778a0a69d3be2618739a31eec86721caa/docs/research/candidates/commitment_residual_triggered_options/pro_packets/20260908_native_cost_reentry_convergence/archive/RESPONSE.md\r\n\r\nThe new consultation adds zero scientific exposure and no experiment budget. One B08 invocation took169s; no additional run is selected. DM advice is to retain the prior boundary with the bounded yield unless the node can specify one distinct justified B discriminator. This advice is not a local family, lifecycle, priority or recast decision. Root dispatches only the new published, full-SHA-bound TASK through the existing Transport; the DM performs no Pro Send.\r\n\r\nThe new task's delivery scope is only docs/research/candidates/commitment_residual_triggered_options/pro_packets/20260908_post_b08_convergence/archive/RESPONSE.md on shared codex/crto plus the immutable delivery-link comment here. Preserve the earlier request, response and comment. Source, main, direction state, experiments and PR merges are outside Pro delivery scope.\r\n\r\n## Prior P68 question (historical scope and status, preserved)\r\n\r\nDecide whether CRTO should select one specified native-cost legal-action learning comparison or retain the current selected-panel family PARK.\r\n\r\nP68 prepared a source-grounded candidate only. The existing competent seed-0 residual negative, comparator-limited seeds 1/2, B06 native KEEP improvement, B07 offsetting action changes, selected-panel ceiling and original MEI .0025 all remain. There is no new result, local reopening, learner budget or lifecycle decision.\r\n\r\nFixed assessment: https://github.com/CartmanFatass/My-paper-code/blob/c9690db8ef340ac8201043183a864454f08c0431/docs/research/candidates/commitment_residual_triggered_options/CRTO_NATIVE_COST_P68_REENTRY_ASSESSMENT_20260908.md\r\n\r\nThe candidate applies one masked expected-native-cost objective to RAW, TRUE_RESIDUAL and CALIBRATED_DERANGEMENT, retaining the old competent RAW as a separate historical comparator floor. Proposed scope is one reused joint seed-0 package, 33/258 update readouts, 774 gate Adam calls, 24768 gate examples and 96 evaluation decisions over the already exposed 16 identities. This is development-informed exploration, not independent replication or repair of both weak seed packages.\r\n\r\nConsultation exposure is zero. Old B04 stage timing projects about 515.38 seconds for one shared invocation, with new objective/current-node/check overhead unmeasured. Proposed 1200-second per-arm and 1500-second shared caps are not allocated. The DM's close-call recommendation is to select this exact B; no aligned gain is the more likely forecast.\r\n\r\nThe committed fixed TASK will authorize Pro only to add docs/research/candidates/commitment_residual_triggered_options/pro_packets/20260908_native_cost_reentry_convergence/archive/RESPONSE.md on existing codex/crto and post the immutable delivery link here. Scientific inputs stay pinned. Root dispatches existing Transport once; the DM reads the full immutable response for intake. Main, source, direction state, experiments and PR merges are outside this delivery scope.\r\n",
